            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An articulatable instrument shaft (242; 274; 322; 354; 414) for a minimally invasive surgical device (228; 260; 312; 344), comprising: a hollow rod (242; 274; 322; 354; 414) having a length and an outer circumference; and a first set of slits (412; 324S; 358) comprising: a first plurality of slits (416; 324S; 358) across the outer circumference dissecting an apex of the hollow rod (414; 322; 354); and a second plurality of slits (418; 326S; 362) oriented 180 degrees around the outer circumference of the hollow rod (414; 322; 354) relative to the first plurality of slits (416; 324S; 358).</p>
